 "about": "Colour tokens of the launcher and (later) the website, . One source of truth: tools/release/theme_tokens.py writes launcher/src/theme_tokens.h from it and checks every text pair below at 4.5:1 or more. Values are libadwaita's named colours (src/stylesheet/_colors.scss and _palette.scss on gitlab.gnome.org, main, read 2026-11-09; facts only, no code); each 'derived' entry is libadwaita's rule (oklab lightness clamped: min 0.5 light, max 0.85 dark) applied to our accent and clipped to sRGB. Colours are #rrggbb or #rrggbbaa (alpha over the 'under' colour of the pair).",
 "accent_bg": "#1e70b9",
 "deviations": [
  "accent_bg: the banner blue #1e70b9 (decision 1) instead of libadwaita's default #3584e4",
  "dim_fg light: alpha 0x8e (about 70 % of the text colour) instead of libadwaita's 55 % (0x70, 3.2:1 on window_bg), so dim text passes 4.5:1",
  "accent_bg_hover/active, destructive_bg_hover/active: 10 % / 20 % black over the fill (libadwaita lightens with 10 % / 20 % of white text, which drops white-on-fill below 4.5:1)",
  "toast_bg/toast_fg: ASSUMPTION, a dark pill in both modes (our value, not read from libadwaita)",
  "toggle_bg: ASSUMPTION, the checked segment of a linked toggle group (the Library filters): raised white in light mode, white at 15 % over the group's button fill in dark (our values, not read from libadwaita)"
 ],
